{
  "name" : "ModelReducer",
  "qualifiedName" : "io.fluxzero.sdk.modeling.ModelReducer",
  "packageName" : "io.fluxzero.sdk.modeling",
  "kind" : "class",
  "modifiers" : [ "final", "public" ],
  "annotations" : [ ],
  "documentation" : " Sole executor for the immutable handler and target knowledge in {@link MutationPlan}.\n <p>\n Interceptor outputs form ordered substeps under one pinned read boundary. Within a substep, payload handlers first\n produce one immutable intermediate state and model handlers then consume that complete state. Handlers within either\n phase never observe partial sibling results; only the composed final state becomes visible to later substeps. This\n class owns handler invocation, result validation, ordering and staged Graph changes for live handling, retry, rebase\n and reconstruction.\n",
